hadiths[24]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19114","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us: Umm Bakr bint al-Miswar ibn Makhrama narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi, from al-Miswar, that Hasan ibn Hasan sent to him proposing to his daughter, so he said to him: Tell him to meet me at the night prayer. He said: So he met him, and al-Miswar praised Allah and extolled Him and said: To proceed, by Allah, there is no kinship nor cause nor marriage tie dearer to me than your cause and marriage tie, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fatima is a piece of me; what constricts her constricts me and what expands her expands me, and kinships on the Day of Resurrection are cut off except my kinship and cause and marriage tie, and with you is her daughter, and had I married you to her that would have constricted her. He said: So he went away excusing him."
"19115","Abu Amir narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Umm Bakr, from al-Miswar, he said: A Jew passed by me while I was standing behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution. He said: So he said: Lift, or uncover, his garment from his back. He said: So I went to lift it, whereupon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) splashed water in my face."
"19117","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar informed us, from al-Zuhri Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama and Marwan ibn al-Hakam, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in the year of Hudaybiyya intending to visit the House, not intending fighting, and he drove with him the sacrificial animals, seventy camels, and the people were seven hundred men, so each camel was for ten. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out until when he was at Usfan he was met by Busr ibn Sufyan al-Kabi, who said: O Messenger of Allah, these Quraysh have heard of your march and have come out with the milch and suckling camels, wearing leopard skins, covenanting with Allah that you shall never enter it upon them by force, and here is Khalid ibn al-Walid with their cavalry advanced to Kura al-Ghamim. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to Quraysh, war has consumed them; what would be upon them had they left me be with the rest of the people? If they strike me that is what they wanted, and if Allah manifests me over them they would enter Islam in full numbers, and if they do not do so they would fight while having strength. What does Quraysh think? By Allah, I shall not cease striving against them for that for which Allah sent me until Allah manifests it for it or this nape is severed. Then he ordered the people and they took to the right between the backs of al-Hamd, upon a road bringing him out at Thaniyyat al-Mirar and Hudaybiyya below Mecca. He said: So he led the army by that road, and when the cavalry of Quraysh saw the dust of the army having diverged from their road they turned back to Quraysh. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out until when he traversed Thaniyyat al-Mirar his she-camel knelt, so the people said: She has balked. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She has not balked, nor is that her nature, but He who restrained the Elephant has restrained her from Mecca. By Allah, Quraysh shall not call me today to any plan in which they ask me for kinship but I shall grant it to them. Then he said to the people: Dismount. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, there is no water in the valley for the people to camp upon. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took an arrow from his quiver and gave it to a man of his companions, who went down into one of those wells and stuck it in it, so water gushed abundantly until the people crowded around it with camels. Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had settled, there came Budayl ibn Warqa with men of Khuzaa, and he said to them like his saying to Busr ibn Sufyan, and they returned to Quraysh and said: O company of Quraysh, you hasten against Muhammad, yet Muhammad has not come for fighting; he has only come visiting this House, honoring its right. So they accused them. Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, said: al-Zuhri said: Khuzaa, during the absence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Muslim and polytheist alike, concealed nothing at Mecca from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: Even if he came only for that, by Allah he shall never enter it upon us by force, nor shall the Arabs speak of that. Then they sent to him Mikraz ibn Hafs ibn al-Akhyaf, one of Banu Amir ibn Luay, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him he said: This is a treacherous man. Then when he reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to him like what he spoke to his companions, then he returned to Quraysh and told them what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him. He said: So they sent to him al-Huls ibn Alqama al-Kinani, who was that day chief of the Ahbash, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him he said: This is of a people who devote themselves, so drive the sacrificial animals before him. So they drove the sacrificial animals, and when he saw the sacrificial animals streaming upon him from the breadth of the valley in their collars, having eaten their halters from long detention from their place, he returned without reaching the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in awe of what he saw, and said: O company of Quraysh, I have seen what may not lawfully be barred: the sacrificial animals in their collars, having eaten their halters from long detention from their place. So they said: Sit, you are only a Bedouin with no knowledge. Then they sent to him Urwa ibn Masud al-Thaqafi, who said: O company of Quraysh, I have seen what befalls from you whoever you send to Muhammad when he comes to you, of harshness and ill speech, and you know that you are father and I am son, and I have heard of what befell you, so I gathered whoever obeyed me of my people, then I came to console you with myself. They said: You speak true; you are not suspect with us. So he went out until he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sat before him and said: O Muhammad, you have gathered the rabble of people, then you came with them to your egg to break it. Quraysh have come out with the milch and suckling camels, wearing leopard skins, covenanting with Allah that you shall never enter it upon them by force. By Allah, it is as if I see these unveiled from you tomorrow. And Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, was seated behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: Suck the clitoris of al-Lat; are we to be unveiled from him? He said: Who is this, O Muhammad? He said: This is Ibn Abi Quhafa. He said: By Allah, were it not for a favor you had with me I would have recompensed you for it, but this is for it. Then he took hold of the beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while al-Mughira ibn Shuba stood at the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in armor. He said: He struck his hand, then said: Hold your hand from the beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before, by Allah, it shall not reach you. He said: Woe to you, how harsh and rude you are. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled. He said: Who is this, O Muhammad? He said: This is your nephew al-Mughira ibn Shuba. He said: O treacherous one, did you wash your filth except yesterday? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to him like what he spoke to his companions, telling him he had not come seeking war. He said: So he rose from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having seen what his companions do with him: he performs no ablution but they rush to it, nor spits spittle but they rush to it, nor falls a hair of his but they take it. So he returned to Quraysh and said: O company of Quraysh, I have come to Kisra in his kingdom, and I have come to Caesar and the Negus in their kingdoms; by Allah, I never saw any king like Muhammad among his companions. I have seen a people who will never surrender him for anything ever; see to your judgment. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had before that sent Khirash ibn Umayya al-Khuzai to Mecca, mounting him on a camel of his called al-Thalab, and when he entered Mecca Quraysh hamstrung it for him and wanted to kill Khirash, but the Ahbash prevented them until he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he called Umar to send him to Mecca, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, I fear Quraysh for myself, and there is none of Banu Adi there to protect me, and Quraysh know my enmity to them and my harshness upon them, but I point you to a man mightier than me: Uthman ibn Affan. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and sent him to Quraysh to tell them he had not come for war and had come visiting this House, honoring its sanctity. So Uthman went out until he came to Mecca, and Aban ibn Said ibn al-As met him, dismounted, carried him before him, rode behind him, and granted him protection until he conveyed the message of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Uthman went until he came to Abu Sufyan and the chiefs of Quraysh and conveyed to them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he sent him with. So they said to Uthman: If you wish to circumambulate the House, do so. So he said: I would not do so until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulates it. He said: So Quraysh detained him with them, and it reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Muslims that Uthman had been killed. Muhammad said: al-Zuhri narrated to me that Quraysh sent Suhayl ibn Amr, one of Banu Amir ibn Luay, saying: Go to Muhammad and make truce with him, and let there be in his truce only that he return from us this year of his, for by Allah the Arabs shall never say he entered it upon us by force. So Suhayl ibn Amr came to him, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him he said: The people have desired truce when they sent this man. Then when he reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they spoke at length and went back and forth until truce ran between them. Then when the matter was joined and nothing remained but the writing, Umar ibn al-Khattab sprang and came to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, is he not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Are we not the Muslims? Are they not the polytheists? He said: Yes. He said: Then why do we yield humiliation in our religion? So Abu Bakr said: O Umar, keep to his stirrup wherever he is, for I testify he is the Messenger of Allah. Umar said: And I testify. Then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, are we not the Muslims? Are they not the polytheists? He said: Yes. He said: Then why do we yield humiliation in our religion? So he said: I am Allah's servant and His Messenger; I shall not oppose His command, nor shall He abandon me. Then Umar said: I kept fasting and giving charity and praying and freeing for what I did, fearing my speech which I spoke that day, until I hoped it would be good. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ali ibn Abi Talib and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Write: In the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate. So Suhayl ibn Amr said: I do not know this, but write: In Your name, O Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Write: In Your name, O Allah. This is what Muhammad the Messenger of Allah has made truce upon with Suhayl ibn Amr. So Suhayl ibn Amr said: Had I witnessed you are the Messenger of Allah I would not have fought you, but write: This is what Muhammad ibn Abd Allah and Suhayl ibn Amr have agreed upon, upon laying down war for ten years, in which people are safe and restrain from one another, upon that whoever comes to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of his companions without permission of his guardian he returns him to them, and whoever comes to Quraysh of those with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they shall not return him to him, and that between us is a covered bosom, and there is no stealth nor treachery. And it was in their condition when they wrote the document that whoever loves to enter the pact of Muhammad and his covenant enters it, and whoever loves to enter the pact of Quraysh and their covenant enters it. So Khuzaa sprang and said: We are with the pact of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his covenant, and Banu Bakr sprang and said: We are in the pact of Quraysh and their covenant. And that you return from us this year of ours and not enter Mecca upon us, and that when next year comes we go out from you and you enter it with your companions and stay among them three days, with you the weapon of the rider; you shall not enter it except with swords in scabbards. Then while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was writing the document, there came to him Abu Jandal ibn Suhayl ibn Amr in irons, having escaped to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had set out not doubting conquest, for a vision the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had seen. Then when they saw what they saw of the truce and return and what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bore upon himself, a grave matter entered the people until they almost perished. Then when Suhayl saw Abu Jandal he rose to him and struck his face, then said: O Muhammad, the case has been concluded between me and you before this one came to you. He said: You speak true. So he rose to him and seized his collar. He said: And Abu Jandal cried at the top of his voice: O company of Muslims, will you return me to the people of idolatry to tempt me in my religion? He said: So the people increased in distress upon what was with them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Jandal, be patient and seek reward, for Allah the Almighty shall make for you and those with you of the oppressed relief and exit. We have concluded between us and the people a truce, giving them upon that and they giving us covenant upon it, and we shall not betray them. He said: So Umar ibn al-Khattab sprang to Abu Jandal and walked beside him saying: Be patient, Abu Jandal, for they are only the polytheists, and the blood of any of them is but the blood of a dog. He said: And he brought the hilt of the sword near to him. He said: He says: I hoped he would take the sword and strike his father with it. He said: So the man spared his father, and the case was executed. Then when they finished the document, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the sanctuary though disturbed in the profane area, he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: O people, sacrifice and shave. He said: So none stood. He said: Then he repeated like it and no man stood, until he repeated like it and no man stood. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned and entered upon Umm Salama and said: O Umm Salama, what is with the people? She said: O Messenger of Allah, what you have seen has entered them, so do not speak to any of them; go to your sacrificial animal wherever it is, sacrifice it and shave, for had you done that the people would do that. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out speaking to no one until he came to his sacrificial animal and sacrificed it, then sat and shaved. So the people rose sacrificing and shaving. He said: Until when they were between Mecca and Medina in the middle of the road, Surat al-Fath was sent down."
"19118","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Numan narrate, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama, that Ali proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl and promised marriage, so Fatima came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your people say you do not anger for your daughters, and Ali has proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and praised Allah and extolled Him and said: Fatima is only a part of me, and I dislike that you tempt her. And he mentioned Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi and lauded him abundantly, and said: The daughter of Allah's Prophet and the daughter of Allah's enemy are not joined. So Ali abandoned that."
"19119","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri: Ali ibn Husayn informed me that al-Miswar ibn Makhrama informed him that Ali ibn Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl while with him was Fatima, daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then when Fatima heard of that she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: Your people say you do not anger for your daughters, and this is Ali marrying the daughter of Abu Jahl. Al-Miswar said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and I heard him when he testified, then he said: To proceed, I married Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi, and he spoke to me and told me true. Fatima bint Muhammad is a part of me, and I dislike that you tempt her. By Allah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah and the daughter of Allah's enemy shall never be joined with one man ever. He said: So Ali left the proposal."
"19120","Yaqub, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Kathir: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhala al-Duali narrated to me that Ibn Shihab narrated to him that Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to him that when they arrived at Medina from Yazid ibn Muawiya after the killing of Husayn ibn Ali, al-Miswar ibn Makhrama met him and said: Have you any need of me you would order me with? He said: So I said to him: No. He said to him: Will you give me the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? For I fear the people may overpower you for it. By Allah, if you give it to me it shall never be reached ever until my soul perishes. Ali ibn Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl upon Fatima, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he addressed the people about that upon this pulpit of his, and I was that day adult, and he said: Fatima is a part of me, and I fear she be tempted in her religion. He said: Then he mentioned a son-in-law of his of Banu Abd Shams and praised him for his marriage to him, doing well. He said: He spoke to me and told me true, and promised me and fulfilled to me. I do not forbid a lawful thing nor permit an unlawful thing, but by Allah the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the daughter of Allah's enemy shall never be joined in one place ever."
"19121","Yaqub narrated to us: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr claimed that Marwan and al-Miswar ibn Makhrama informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood when the delegation of Hawazin came to him as Muslims asking to return to them their properties and captives. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: With me are those you see, and the speech dearest to me is the truest, so choose one of the two parties: either the captives or the property, and I had waited for you. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had awaited them ten-odd nights when he returned from Taif. Then when it became clear to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would return to them only one of the two parties, they said: Then we choose our captives. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among the Muslims and praised Allah the Almighty as He deserves, then said: To proceed, your brothers have come repentant, and I have seen fit to return to them their captives, so whoever of you loves to make that pleasant let him do, and whoever of you loves to be upon his share until we give it to him from the first that Allah the Almighty grants us, let him do. So the people said: We have made that pleasant for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: We do not know who of you permitted in that of who did not permit, so return until your headmen raise to us your affair. So the people gathered and their headmen spoke to them, then they returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him they had made it pleasant and permitted. This is what reached me about the captives of Hawazin."
"19122","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us that al-Miswar ibn Makhrama informed him that Amr ibn Awf al-Ansari, an ally of Banu Amir ibn Luay who had witnessed Badr with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah to Bahrayn to bring its tribute, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had made truce with the people of Bahrayn and appointed over them al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami. So Abu Ubayda arrived with wealth from Bahrayn, then he mentioned the hadith, meaning like the hadith of Mamar."
"19123","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama, he said: The Ansar heard that Abu Ubayda had arrived with wealth from Bahrayn, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sent him over Bahrayn, so they attended with the Messenger of Allah the dawn prayer. Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished they confronted him, and when he saw them he smiled and said: Perhaps you heard that Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah has arrived, and has arrived with wealth. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He said: Receive glad tidings and hope for good. By Allah, it is not poverty I fear for you, but when the world is poured upon you and you compete in it as those before you competed in it."
"19124","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, that al-Miswar ibn Makhrama informed him [no further text in the source]."
"19125","He said: And Ishaq, meaning Ibn al-Tabba, narrated to us, he said: Malik informed me, from Hisham, from his father, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama, that Subaya al-Aslamiyya gave birth after her husband's death by nights, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: You have become lawful, so marry."
"19126","Hammad ibn Usama narrated to us: Hisham informed us, from his father, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama, that Subaya al-Aslamiyya, her husband died while she was pregnant, and she remained only nights until she gave birth. Then when she finished her confinement she was proposed to, so she sought the permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for marriage, and he permitted her to marry, so she married."
"19127","Abu Muawiya narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Asim ibn Umar, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama, he said: Subaya gave birth, then he mentioned the hadith."
"19128","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama and Marwan, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) garlanded the sacrificial animals and marked them at Dhu al-Hulayfa and entered ihram from there for umra. He shaved at Hudaybiyya in his umra and ordered his companions with that, and he sacrificed at Hudaybiyya before shaving and ordered his companions with that."
"19129","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Awf ibn al-Harith, nephew of Aisha through her mother, that Aisha narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr said, about a sale or gift she had given: By Allah, Aisha shall desist or I shall interdict her. So Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: Did he say this? They said: Yes. She said: It is upon me a vow to Allah never to speak a word to Ibn al-Zubayr. So Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr sought the intercession of al-Miswar ibn Makhrama and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth, both of Banu Zuhra, then he mentioned the hadith. And al-Miswar and Abd al-Rahman set to adjuring Aisha but to speak to him and accept from him, saying to her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had forbidden what she knew of desertion: it is not lawful for a Muslim to desert his brother above three nights."
"19130","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: al-Awzai narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from al-Tufayl ibn al-Harith, a man of Azd Shanua and brother of Aisha through her mother Umm Ruman, then he mentioned the hadith. So he sought help upon her with al-Miswar ibn Makhrama and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth. So they sought permission upon her and she permitted them, and they spoke to her and adjured her by Allah and kinship and the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): It is not lawful for a Muslim man to desert his brother above three."
"19131","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri: Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Tufayl, nephew of Aisha wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through her mother, informed me that Aisha narrated to him, then he mentioned the hadith."
"19132","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Marwan and al-Miswar ibn Makhrama, one adding to the other: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in the year of Hudaybiyya with ten-odd hundred of his companions, and when he was at Dhu al-Hulayfa he garlanded the sacrificial animals and marked them and entered ihram from there. And Sufyan once said: For umra, and he did not name al-Miswar. And he sent a scout of his ahead of him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) travelled until when [the source breaks off here]."
"19133","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Irak, that he heard Marwan at the pilgrimage season say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut for a shield, and a camel is better than a shield."
"19134","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: al-Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Mulayka narrated to me, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while upon the pulpit say: The sons of Hisham ibn al-Mughira sought my permission to marry their daughter to Ali ibn Abi Talib, so I do not permit them. Then he said: I do not permit. Then he said: I do not permit. My daughter is only a part of me; what troubles her troubles me and what harms her harms me."
"19135","Hashim narrated to us: Layth narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Mulayka narrated to me, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama, he said: Cloaks buttoned with gold were gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he divided them among his companions. So Makhrama said: O Miswar, take us to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for it has been mentioned to me that he divided cloaks. So we set out, and he said: Enter and call him for me. He said: So I entered and called him to him, and he came out to me wearing a cloak of them. He said: I hid this for you, O Makhrama. He said: So he looked at it and said: Are you pleased? So he gave it to him."
"19136","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar: al-Zuhri said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama and Marwan ibn al-Hakam, each confirming the hadith of his companion, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out at the time of Hudaybiyya with ten-odd hundred of his companions, until when they were at Dhu al-Hulayfa the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) garlanded the sacrificial animals and marked them and entered ihram for umra, and he sent ahead of him a scout of his of Khuzaa to tell him of Quraysh. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) travelled until when he was at Ghadir al-Ashtat near Usfan, his Khuzaite scout came to him and said: I have left Kab ibn Luay and Amir ibn Luay having gathered for you the Ahbash and gathered for you multitudes, and they will fight you and bar you from the House. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Advise me; do you see that we incline to the offspring of those who aided them and strike them? If they sit they sit bereaved and despoiled, and if they escape. And Yahya ibn Said said, from Ibn al-Mubarak: grieved. And if they bend (?), it is a neck Allah has cut. Or do you see that we make for the House, and whoever bars us from it we fight him? So Abu Bakr said: Allah and His Messenger know best, O Prophet of Allah; we came only performing umra, we did not come to fight anyone, but whoever stands between us and the House we fight him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then proceed. Al-Zuhri said: And Abu Hurayra used to say: I never saw anyone at all more consulting to his companions than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Zuhri said, in the hadith of al-Miswar ibn Makhrama and Marwan ibn al-Hakam: So they journeyed until when they were on part of the road the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Khalid ibn al-Walid is at al-Ghamim with cavalry of Quraysh as vanguard, so take to the right. By Allah, Khalid did not perceive them until there he was with the dust of the army. So he galloped off warning Quraysh. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) travelled until when he was at the pass from which he descends upon them, his mount knelt. And Yahya ibn Said said, from Ibn al-Mubarak: His mount knelt with her. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hal, hal. But she persisted. So they said: al-Qaswa has balked. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Qaswa has not balked, nor is that her nature, but He who restrained the Elephant has restrained her. Then he said: By Him in whose Hand is my soul, they shall not ask me any plan in which they honor the sanctities of Allah but I shall grant it to them. Then he drove her and she sprang with him. He said: So he turned from her until he camped at the farthest Hudaybiyya upon a scant-water hollow which people scoop little by little. The people soon drained it, so thirst was complained of to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he drew an arrow from his quiver, then ordered them to place it in it. He said: By Allah, it kept gushing for them with abundance until they departed from it. He said: Then while they were so, there came Budayl ibn Warqa al-Khuzai with men of his people, who were a trusted confidants of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of Tihama. And he said: I have left Kab ibn Luay and Amir ibn Luay camped at the waters of Hudaybiyya with them the milch and suckling camels, and they will fight you and bar you from the House. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have not come to fight anyone, but we came performing umra. Quraysh have been exhausted by war and it has harmed them. If they wish I shall grant them a truce-period, and they leave me be with the people. If I prevail, then if they wish to enter into what the people entered into they do, otherwise they have rested. And if they refuse, then by Him in whose Hand is my soul I shall fight them upon this affair of mine until my nape is severed or Allah executes His command. Yahya said, from Ibn al-Mubarak: Until it is severed. He said: Then if they wish we grant them a period. Budayl said: I shall convey what you say. So he went until he came to Quraysh and said: We have come to you from this man, and we heard him say a saying; if you wish we present it to you. Their fools said: We have no need for you to tell us of him anything. And their men of judgment said: Bring what you heard him say. He said: I heard him say such and such. So he told them what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. So Urwa ibn Masud al-Thaqafi stood and said: O people, are you not the father? They said: Yes. He said: Am I not the son? They said: Yes. He said: Do you suspect me? They said: No. He said: Do you not know that I summoned the people of Ukaz, and when they lagged upon me I came to you with my household and whoever obeyed me? They said: Yes. So he said: He has offered you a right-minded plan, so accept it and let me go to him. So they said: Go to him. So he came to him. He said: So he spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to him like his saying to Budayl. So Urwa said thereupon: O Muhammad, tell me: if you exterminate your people, have you heard of any of the Arabs who destroyed his folk before you? And if it be the other, by Allah I see faces and I see rabble of people likely to flee and leave you. So Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: Suck the clitoris of al-Lat; shall we flee from him and leave him? So he said: Who is this? They said: Abu Bakr. He said: By Him in whose Hand is my soul, were it not for a favor you had with me I had not yet repaid you, I would have answered you. And he spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and whenever he spoke to him he seized his beard, while al-Mughira ibn Shuba stood at the head of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the sword and upon him the helmet. And whenever Urwa reached with his hand to the beard of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he struck his hand with the sword-edge and said: Keep your hand from the beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Urwa lifted his hand. So he said: Who is this? They said: al-Mughira ibn Shuba. He said: O treacherous one, am I not striving in your treachery? For al-Mughira had accompanied a people in ignorance and killed them and taken their properties, then came and accepted Islam. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for Islam I accept, and as for the property I have nothing to do with it. Then Urwa set to eyeing the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his eye. He said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat no spittle but it fell in the palm of a man of them and he rubbed his face and skin with it, and when he ordered them they hastened to his order, and when he performed ablution they almost fought over his ablution water, and when they spoke they lowered their voices with him and did not stare at him in honor of him. So he returned to his companions and said: O people, by Allah I have come as envoy to kings, and I have come to Caesar and Kisra and the Negus; by Allah, I never saw any king his companions honor as the companions of Muhammad honor Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). By Allah, he spits no spittle but it falls in the palm of a man of them and he rubs his face and skin with it, and when he orders them they hasten to his order, and when he performs ablution they almost fight over his ablution water, and when they speak they lower their voices with him and do not stare at him in honor of him. He has offered you a right-minded plan, so accept it. So a man of Banu Kinana said: Let me go to him. So they said: Go to him. Then when he looked upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is so-and-so, of a people who honor the sacrificial camels, so drive them for him. So they were driven for him, and the people received him chanting the talbiya. Then when he saw that he said: Glory be to Allah, these may not be barred from the House. He said: Then when he returned to his companions he said: I saw the sacrificial camels garlanded and marked, and I did not see they be barred from the House. So a man of them called Mikraz ibn Hafs stood and said: Let me go to him. So they said: Go to him. Then when he looked upon them the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is Mikraz, a profligate man. So he spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and while he spoke to him there came Suhayl ibn Amr. Mamar said: And Ayyub informed me, from Ikrima, that when Suhayl came the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your affair has been eased. Al-Zuhri said in his hadith: So Suhayl ibn Amr came and said: Come, write between us and you a document. So he called the scribe. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Write: In the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate. So Suhayl said: As for the Merciful, by Allah I do not know what it is. And Ibn al-Mubarak said: What it is. But write: In Your name, O Allah, as you used to write. So the Muslims said: By Allah, we write it only: In the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Write: In Your name, O Allah. Then he said: This is what Muhammad the Messenger of Allah has decreed. So Suhayl said: By Allah, had we known you are the Messenger of Allah we would not have barred you from the House nor fought you, but write: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, I am the Messenger of Allah though you deny me. Write: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah. Al-Zuhri said: And that is for his saying: They shall not ask me any plan in which they honor the sanctities of Allah but I shall grant them it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon that you leave between us and the House and we circumambulate it. So Suhayl said: By Allah, the Arabs shall not say we were taken under strain, but for you is next year. So he wrote. So Suhayl said: Upon that no man of us comes to you, though upon your religion, but you return him to us. So the Muslims said: Glory be to Allah, how is one returned to the polytheists having come as Muslim? Then while they were so, there came Abu Jandal ibn Suhayl ibn Amr hobbling. And Yahya said, from Ibn al-Mubarak: clanking in his fetters, having come out from lower Mecca until he threw himself among the Muslims. So Suhayl said: This, O Muhammad, is the first I make terms with you upon: that you return him to me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have not yet concluded the document. He said: Then by Allah I shall never make truce with you upon anything ever. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then grant him to me. He said: I am not granting him to you. He said: Yes, do so. He said: I shall not do so. Mikraz said: Yes, we have granted him to you. So Abu Jandal said: O company of Muslims, am I returned to the polytheists having come as Muslim? Do you not see what I have met? For he had been tormented a severe torment for Allah. So Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, said: So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Are you not Allah's Prophet? He said: Yes. I said: Are we not upon the truth and our enemy upon falsehood? He said: Yes. I said: Then why do we yield vileness in our religion? He said: I am Allah's Messenger, and I do not disobey Him, and He is my Helper. I said: Did you not tell us we shall come to the House and circumambulate it? He said: Yes. He said: Did I tell you that you come to it this year? I said: No. He said: Then you shall come to it and circumambulate it. He said: So I came to Abu Bakr, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, and said: O Abu Bakr, is this not Allah's Prophet in truth? He said: Yes. I said: Are we not upon the truth and our enemy upon falsehood? He said: Yes. I said: Then why do we yield vileness in our religion? He said: O man, he is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he does not disobey his Lord the Almighty, and He is his Helper, so hold fast. And Yahya ibn Said said: By his stirrup. And he said: Circle by his stirrup until you die. For by Allah he is upon the truth. I said: Did he not tell us we shall come to the House and circumambulate it? He said: Yes. He said: Did he tell you that he comes to it this year? I said: No. He said: Then you shall come to it and circumambulate it. Al-Zuhri said: Umar said: So I did deeds for that. He said: Then when he finished the conclusion of the document the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Stand, sacrifice, then shave. He said: By Allah, no man of them stood until he said that three times. Then when none of them stood he stood and entered upon Umm Salama and mentioned to her what he met of the people. So Umm Salama said: O Messenger of Allah, do you desire that? Go out, then do not speak to any of them a word until you sacrifice your camel and call your barber to shave you. So he rose and went out and spoke to none of them until he did that: he sacrificed his offering and called his barber. Then when they saw that they stood and sacrificed, and some began shaving others until some almost killed others in grief. Then believing women came to him, so Allah the Almighty sent down: O you who believe, when the believing women come to you as emigrants, until He reached: with the ties of disbelieving women. He said: So Umar that day divorced two wives of his who were his in idolatry. So Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan married one of them, and the other Safwan ibn Umayya. Then he returned to Medina, and there came to him Abu Basir, a man of Quraysh, Muslim. And Yahya said, from Ibn al-Mubarak: So there arrived to him Abu Basir ibn Usayd al-Thaqafi, Muslim, emigrant. So al-Akhnas ibn Shariq, a disbelieving man of Banu Amir ibn Luay, hired, and a freedman with him, and wrote with them to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking fulfillment. So they sent in pursuit of him two men, saying: The covenant you made for us therein. So he handed him to the two men. So they went out with him until they reached Dhu al-Hulayfa with him, and they camped eating dates of theirs. So Abu Basir said to one of the two men: By Allah, I see your sword, O so-and-so, is good. So the other drew it and said: Yes, by Allah it is good; I have tried it with it, then tried. So Abu Basir said: Show me to look at it. So he enabled him of it, and he struck him until he grew cold, and the other fled until he came to Medina and entered the mosque running. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one has seen terror. Then when he reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: By Allah, my companion is killed, and I am to be killed. So Abu Basir came and said: O Prophet of Allah, Allah has fulfilled your liability; you returned me to them, then Allah saved me from them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to his mother, a kindler of war, had he supporters. Then when he heard that he knew he would return him to them. So he went out until he came to the seashore. He said: And Abu Jandal ibn Suhayl escaped and joined Abu Basir. So no Muslim man of Quraysh went out but joined Abu Basir, until a band gathered of them. He said: By Allah, they hear of no caravan going out for Quraysh to Sham but they waylay it, killing them and taking their properties. So Quraysh sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) adjuring him by Allah and kinship to send to them: whoever comes to him is safe. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to them. So Allah the Almighty sent down: And He it is who withheld their hands from you and your hands from them, until He reached: the zealotry of ignorance. And their zealotry was that they did not affirm he is Allah's Prophet, nor affirmed In the name of Allah the Merciful the Compassionate, and stood between him and the House."
"19137","Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama and Marwan ibn al-Hakam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out at the time of Hudaybiyya with ten-odd hundred. Then he mentioned the hadith. He said: And from here it is attached to the hadith of al-Zuhri from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad. He said: And Abu Basir said to al-Amiri, with him his sword: I see this sword of yours, O brother of Banu Amir, is good. He said: Yes, indeed. He said: Show me to look at it. He said: So he handed it to him. So Abu Basir drew it, then struck al-Amiri until he killed him. And the freedman fled hastening toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he entered, they claimed, upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the mosque, the gravel humming from the severity of his running. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him when he saw him: This one has seen terror. Then he mentioned like the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq. He said: Then when the disbelievers of Quraysh saw that, riders of them rode to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your truce-period avails nothing, while we are killed and our properties plundered. We ask you to admit into your truce those of us who accepted Islam and to protect them and restrain fighting them from us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that. And Allah the Almighty sent down: And He it is who withheld their hands from you and your hands from them. So he read until he reached: the zealotry of ignorance."
"19138","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us: Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Umm Bakr and Jafar, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi, from al-Miswar, he said: Hasan ibn Hasan sent to al-Miswar proposing to a daughter of his. He said to him: You will meet me at the night prayer. So he met him, and al-Miswar praised Allah and said: There is no cause nor kinship nor marriage tie dearer to me than your kinship and marriage tie, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fatima is an offshoot of me; what expands her expands me and what constricts her constricts me. And kinships and causes are cut off on the Day of Resurrection except my kinship and cause. And under you is her daughter, and had I married you it would have constricted her. So he went away excusing him."
